user32: Keep the default item's mark when ModifyMenu changes the item.

ModifyMenu sets an item's whole state from its flags, and MF_DEFAULT is
not one of the flags it accepts, so it cleared the default mark of the
item it changed. Programs that set the default item, then rename the
menu's items for a language with ModifyMenu, lose it: Ditto, the
clipboard manager, does this when its language is not English, so a click
on its notification icon, which runs the menu's default item, does
nothing. On Windows the same program opens its window, so ModifyMenu
leaves the mark alone there; Wine's own test only checks that it cannot
set it.

Status: not for WineHQ as it stands. This patch was written with an LLM,
and WineHQ does not accept LLM-generated code. No WineHQ bug describes
this yet (bugs.winehq.org searched for ModifyMenu and MFS_DEFAULT on
2026-10-21).
---
--- a/dlls/user32/menu.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/menu.c
@@ -459,7 +459,7 @@
 BOOL WINAPI ModifyMenuW( HMENU hMenu, UINT pos, UINT flags,
                          UINT_PTR id, LPCWSTR str )
 {
-    MENUITEMINFOW mii;
+    MENUITEMINFOW mii, old;
 
     if (IS_STRING_ITEM(flags))
         TRACE("%p %d %04x %04Ix %s\n", hMenu, pos, flags, id, debugstr_w(str) );
@@ -467,6 +467,11 @@
         TRACE("%p %d %04x %04Ix %p\n", hMenu, pos, flags, id, str );
 
     MENU_mnu2mnuii( flags, id, str, &mii);
+    /* ModifyMenu neither sets nor clears the default item: keep its mark */
+    old.cbSize = sizeof(old);
+    old.fMask = MIIM_STATE;
+    if (GetMenuItemInfoW( hMenu, pos, (flags & MF_BYPOSITION) != 0, &old ))
+        mii.fState |= old.fState & MFS_DEFAULT;
     return NtUserThunkedMenuItemInfo( hMenu, pos, flags, NtUserSetMenuItemInfo, &mii, NULL );
 }
 
